dialogue desert_party_talk
title: What the shards are
trigger: ThemeStart desert
speaker commander $commander
speaker trusted $trusted
speaker alchemist - name=Alchemist portrait=alchemist

node a commander
  Red earth, and horns taller than towers. Did these fall? My hand aches when I go near them.
  -> b

node b alchemist
  Some of them are the Manalith's own shell, shed as it comes. The Choir digs it out and the Ember pray for the rest. And that ache is your mana answering. Everyone's runs thin. Yours is whole. I've never seen that.
  * You've watched my hand all morning. Say it. -> speak
    if: TrustAtLeast $trusted 25
  * Whole, and I don't know why. Let's keep moving.

node speak trusted
  The ache. I've seen people go near a shard and come back thin. You come back steadier. I don't understand it, and I don't need to. I just want to be close when it matters.
  * Stay close, then. If my hand starts to shake, you'll be the one I tell. -> close
    do: AddTrust $trusted 6
  * Stay near. Whatever this is, I'd rather not find out alone. -> near
    do: AddTrust $trusted 4

node close trusted
  The one you tell. I'll hold you to that, Commander.

node near trusted
  Not alone. That's an easy promise to keep.
